<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) DROPS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES THUR.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) DROPS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES THUR.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek gasoline prices will be lowered by 1.20 drachmas per litre and transport diesel will drop by 0.50 drachmas, effective on Thursday and for one week, Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The price of diesel used as heating fuel will go up by 0.80 drachmas per litre.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after lower world gasoline prices, down by $5.6 per metric tonne, lower diesel prices, down by $2.3 and a stable dollar/drachma exchange rate. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
